libx264 takes 8-bit 4:2:0 in the limited range only (yuv420p, nv12, nv21), what
browsers play. Without it, an upload in 10 bit (HEVC of a phone), in 4:2:2
(MJPEG of a camera) or in 4:4:4 (a screen recording) becomes H.264 High 10,
High 4:2:2 or High 4:4:4 when the command has no -pix_fmt yuv420p (KVS puts it
in front of the options of a format that have no -pix_fmt and no hwaccel):
Safari and iPhones play none of these, other browsers not everywhere. With this
list ffmpeg converts such input into 8-bit 4:2:0 itself (an explicit -pix_fmt
of another format is turned into yuv420p, with a warning).

The range: since FFmpeg 7.1 ffmpeg keeps the range of the input ("YUV
colorspace negotiation for codecs and filters" in its Changelog), so -pix_fmt
yuv420p no longer means the limited range: an MJPEG of a camera or a phone
video in the full range became H.264 in the full range (yuvj420p, pc), which not
every player shows right (Firefox did not until 91). With the limited range only,
as the encoder mpeg4 declares, ffmpeg converts it, and the sites get what FFmpeg
7.0 and older gave them. -color_range pc still gives the full range.

--- a/libavcodec/libx264.c
+++ b/libavcodec/libx264.c
@@ -1481,6 +1481,17 @@
 #endif
     AV_PIX_FMT_NONE
 };
+/* What browsers play: 8-bit 4:2:0. With only these formats ffmpeg converts any
+ * other input into 8-bit 4:2:0 itself, without -pix_fmt yuv420p in the command.
+ * No yuvj420p: it is the full range (below). */
+static const enum AVPixelFormat pix_fmts_8bit_420[] = {
+    AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P,
+    AV_PIX_FMT_NV12,
+#ifdef X264_CSP_NV21
+    AV_PIX_FMT_NV21,
+#endif
+    AV_PIX_FMT_NONE
+};
 #if CONFIG_LIBX264RGB_ENCODER
 static const enum AVPixelFormat pix_fmts_8bit_rgb[] = {
     AV_PIX_FMT_BGR0,
@@ -1625,8 +1636,12 @@
     .flush            = X264_flush,
     .close            = X264_close,
     .defaults         = x264_defaults,
-    CODEC_PIXFMTS_ARRAY(pix_fmts_all),
-    .color_ranges     = AVCOL_RANGE_MPEG | AVCOL_RANGE_JPEG,
+    CODEC_PIXFMTS_ARRAY(pix_fmts_8bit_420),
+    /* The limited range only: since FFmpeg 7.1 the range of the input is kept,
+     * and -pix_fmt yuv420p made full range H.264 of a full range upload (MJPEG
+     * of a camera, a phone video); ffmpeg now converts it, as for mpeg4.
+     * -color_range pc still gives the full range. */
+    .color_ranges     = AVCOL_RANGE_MPEG,
     .caps_internal  = FF_CODEC_CAP_INIT_CLEANUP | FF_CODEC_CAP_AUTO_THREADS
 #if X264_BUILD < 158
                       | FF_CODEC_CAP_NOT_INIT_THREADSAFE
